      "message": "\u003e is there a need for the call to trace_.._enabled()?\n\nNo, there is no logic difference. Putting everything under the *_enabled() thing isn\u0027t a must-have, it\u0027s just an optimization to avoid the if (target \u003e\u003d 0) when the hook is disabled. That is, *_enabled() is a static key, which is faster to check than a standard condition. It\u0027s possible the compiler will figure it out on its own, but who trusts compilers ;) ?",
